BEGIN_DESC
AtmoFX layers (needs the AtmoFX fork of D3D9Client). Noon light, sun 40 deg up. The probe sinks from 560 km - in the photochemical haze - at 2 km/s (real time, ~2 min) through the ammonia deck (445-475 km), the clear gap, the brown ammonium hydrosulfide deck (390-415 km) down to the water clouds (330-370 km), where the light is nearly gone and lightning flickers. Layers in Config\AtmoFX_Volume.cfg.
Numpad8/2 climb/descend (stops the descent, Shift x10), Numpad4/6/5 drift. Ctrl+arrows / right mouse - look around (up at the deck above, down into the depths).
END_DESC

BEGIN_ENVIRONMENT
  System Sol
  Date MJD 60970.5
END_ENVIRONMENT

BEGIN_FOCUS
  Ship Probe
END_FOCUS

BEGIN_CAMERA
  TARGET Probe
  MODE Cockpit
  FOV 60.00
END_CAMERA

BEGIN_HUD
  TYPE Surface
END_HUD

BEGIN_SHIPS
Probe:AtmoProbe
  STATUS Landed Jupiter
  POS 0.0000000 -15.0000000
  HEADING 0.00
  TOUR 560 345 2.0
  DRIFT 0.2
  SUNELEV 40
  CLOUDS 0
END
END_SHIPS
